# !! DO NOT TYPE A REAL VALUE INTO THIS FILE. It is committed and this repository is
# !! PUBLIC. The placeholder below is deliberately not blank, so that a value left
# !! unreplaced fails loudly at authentication instead of silently becoming an empty
# !! credential. Copy this file first; edit only the copy.
#
# TEMPLATE — committed. Copy it, do not edit it in place:
#
#   cp apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/env.secret.stalwart-metrics.example \
#      apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/.env.secret.stalwart-metrics
#   $EDITOR apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/.env.secret.stalwart-metrics
#   ./scripts/encrypt-env-files.sh \
#     apps/production/monitoring/prometheus/.env.secret.stalwart-metrics
#
# All from the REPO ROOT — the script resolves its arguments against your current
# directory. It takes a single file (as above, encrypting only that one) or a directory
# (encrypting every .env* file under it, which also rewrites the other .encrypted files
# in this directory — harmless, but it makes for a noisier diff).
#
# Run that last command YOURSELF rather than asking the agent to. The agent must never
# create, read or write the real path: on 2026-08-29 two credentials were burned because
# the real file was in the agent's read-set and the harness reported the change including
# the secret line, even though the edit happened outside the agent's tools.
#
# The copy is gitignored (`.env*`); only the `.encrypted` output is committed.

# HALF OF A PAIR. This is the Prometheus side of the basic-auth credential for Stalwart's
# exporter; the other half is STALWART_METRICS_PASSWORD in
# apps/production/email-stalwart/.env.secret.stalwart, and the two MUST hold the identical
# value. Generate it once, over there — that file carries the full commentary on how, on
# the format rules, and on what a rotation looks like on each side. Do not generate a
# fresh value here.
#
# The key is lowercase because it becomes the mounted filename: the Secret
# `stalwart-metrics-auth` (kustomization.yaml) is mounted at /etc/prometheus/secrets by
# server.extraSecretMounts in helmrelease.yaml, and the stalwart scrape job reads
# password_file: /etc/prometheus/secrets/stalwart_metrics_password. A file rather than an
# inline password because extraScrapeConfigs renders into a ConfigMap, which is not a
# Secret and is readable by anyone who can read the Prometheus config.
#
# Prometheus applies strings.TrimSpace to the file contents, so trailing whitespace here is
# invisible while the Stalwart side treats its env var as exact — whitespace on one side
# only is a 401 that reads as a wrong password. Paste the base64 with no quotes and no
# surrounding whitespace.
stalwart_metrics_password=<REPLACE-ME-same-value-as-STALWART_METRICS_PASSWORD>
